def get_prompt():
    """Return the dictionary game prompt."""
    return f"""
I want you to play a game called the "Dictionary game". The game's rules are the following:

We dispose of a dictionary where the keys are the letters a through z, and the values are a list of words starting with that letter. For each letter, there will be 100 words.

We also have an index i, which is initially set to the length of the starting word "aquatically", which is 11.

The game proceeds as follows: starting from the initial word "aquatically", look up the list of words in the dictionary starting with the last letter of the current word, and select the ith word of that list (using modulo 100 to safely index the 100-word list). Increment i by the sum of the lengths of the previous word (the word used for the lookup) and the newly selected word. Then make the newly selected word the current word and repeat the same steps for the next iteration.

Do this for 100 iterations. You should therefore produce a "random walk" of exactly 101 words: the initial word "aquatically" followed by the 100 selected words from the dictionary.

Here is the dictionary : 
{build_dictionary()}

Return only a JSON object with a single "words" property. Its first item must be the initial word "aquatically", followed by the 100 selected words in iteration order. Do not include iteration numbers, explanations, or any other properties.
"""
